```json
{
  "dependee_register": {"register_name": "RCTL", "subfield_name_abbreviation": "EN", "bit_range": "1", "value": "0"},
  "dependent_register": {"register_name": "MRQC", "subfield_name_abbreviation": "MRxQueue", "bit_range": "1:0", "value": "any"},
  "relevant_sentence": "This field can be modified only when receive to host is not enabled (RCTL.EN = 0).",
  "dependency_type": "software",
  "linear_type_enforceable": true
}
```
**Reason**: *You may only write MRQC when RCTL.EN=0.* This is classical linear state: generate a token by disabling RCTL.EN; you must spend that token to write MRQC.

